MODULE archive

FUNCTION extract asset into empty staging directory
    require a positive total expansion limit
    select raw, ZIP, tar.gz, tar.bz2, or tar.xz extraction
    reject unsupported formats
    after extraction, require every declared executable as a regular file

FUNCTION extract archive entries
    clean forward-slash paths and remove the declared leading components
    skip entries removed completely by stripping
    reject absolute paths, backslashes, parent traversal, duplicate output
        paths, symbolic links, hard links, devices, and other special entries
    reject more than 100,000 archive entries
    create only contained directories and new regular files
    sanitize permissions to user-readable files and executable bits when set
    count all written bytes and stop when the configured limit is exceeded
    synchronize and close each output file
    require every declared binary directory, then make each declared executable
        mode 0755 and require it to be a regular file

FUNCTION extract raw asset
    copy the verified archive object to its declared contained path as an
        executable regular file under the same expansion limit
